info.description:
These are the available filter operators for "filters" query parameter:
    "_in" - Matches values in an array. => {"name": {"_in": ["John", "Jane"]}}
    "_nin" - Matches values not in an array. => {"name": {"_nin": ["Peter", "Jack"]}}
    "_lt" - Matches values less than given value. => {"age": {"_lt": 20}}
    "_lte" - Matches values less than or equal to given value. => {"age": {"_lte": 20}}
    "_gt" - Matches values greater than given value. => {"age": {"_gt": 20}}
    "_gte" - Matches values greater than or equal to given value. => {"age": {"_gte": 20}}
    "_eq" - Matches values equal to given value. => {"age": {"_eq": 20}}
    "_ne" - Matches values not equal to given value. => {"age": {"_ne": 20}}
    "_ilike" - Matches values using case-insensitive LIKE search (partial matching). => {"name": {"_ilike": "John"}}
    "_like" - Matches values using case-sensitive LIKE search (partial matching). => {"name": {"_like": "John"}}
